  :notes "Implements the wave48-accepted recovery-smoke shard inside scripts/check-v3-request-flow-smoke.mjs. Single-file change; no edits to crates/, packages/, V3 blueprint or its checkers, or wave48 artifacts.\n\nWhat --restart-during-dispatch does (PLAN-ONLY):\n  - Validation gate: validateOpts() refuses unless BOTH --live-ipc and --execute-real-dispatch are also present. The CLI exits 2 with a clear diagnostic when --restart-during-dispatch is supplied alone, paired only with --live-ipc, or paired only with --execute-real-dispatch.\n  - Live path (when all three flags are on): after the existing wave47 execute_plan_real_dispatch step succeeds, the smoke captures delegated_board_task_id + delegated_board_task_assignee from realStep, calls buildRestartRecoveryPlan(), attaches the plan as summary.restart_recovery_plan, and pushes a 'restart_recovery_plan' step (kind=review, ok=true, live_executed=false) onto summary.steps.\n  - The plan is a structured 5-step recovery sequence: (1) capture_pre_restart_state, (2) restart_daemon (kind=side_effect, live_only=true), (3) observe_pin_clear, (4) observe_redispatch, (5) assert_recovery_proof. Each step has step/name/kind/action/expectation fields plus the slot/task identifiers reused as expectation references.\n  - parent_run_command field publishes the exact preferred (launchctl kickstart -k) and fallback (pgrep+kill -TERM) shell commands. The script itself NEVER kills the daemon, never invokes launchctl, never sends SIGTERM. The actual restart is parent-driven so the operator can review the plan before touching the supervisor.\n  - Pattern-card 'opt-in-live-smoke' compliance: default invocation stays read-only; --live-ipc without --execute-real-dispatch still stops before dispatch; --live-ipc + --execute-real-dispatch (without --restart-during-dispatch) still behaves exactly as wave47.\n\nWhat remains parent-run / live-only:\n  - Step 2 'restart_daemon' is marked live_only=true and is NOT executed by this script. Operators run the launchctl kickstart command manually after reviewing the plan.\n  - Step 3 'observe_pin_clear' and step 4 'observe_redispatch' instruct the operator to poll mission_board_get(taskId=...) every 5s for up to 5 minutes; the smoke does not implement a long-running poll loop because that would require either a parent-supplied confirmation flag (intentionally omitted in this shard per the contract's 'do not run a live daemon restart unless the parent explicitly asks') or a daemon-side restart trigger.\n  - The wave48 acceptance command 'node scripts/check-v3-request-flow-smoke.mjs --live-ipc --execute-real-dispatch --restart-during-dispatch --cleanup --json' is parent-driven and was NOT executed in this task. Running it produces a successful execute_plan_real_dispatch followed by a 'restart_recovery_plan' review step; live verification of the recovery itself is up to the parent.\n\nDry-fixture cases added (composed into the existing runFixtures summary; total grew 9 -> 16):\n  Validation cases (validateOpts):\n    1. default opts validate ok (no restart flag)\n    2. live-ipc only without restart flag still validates ok (preserves wave43 contract)\n    3. restart-during-dispatch alone is rejected (errorContains: 'requires --live-ipc')\n    4. restart-during-dispatch + live-ipc without real-dispatch is rejected (errorContains: 'requires --execute-real-dispatch')\n    5. restart-during-dispatch + execute-real-dispatch without live-ipc is rejected (errorContains: 'requires --live-ipc')\n    6. restart-during-dispatch with both gates validates ok\n  Plan structural case (buildRestartRecoveryPlan):\n    7. With synthetic delegated_board_task_id + pre_restart_assignee + request_id + repo_root, the planner emits exactly 5 steps in the expected order, each with non-empty action/expectation strings, live_executed=false, requires_flags includes all three flags, parent_run_command.preferred references launchctl, and pre_restart_state echoes the synthetic inputs back.\n\nBackward compatibility evidence:\n  - 'node scripts/check-v3-request-flow-smoke.mjs --dry-fixture' exit=0 (16 fixtures, 6 states, 6 decisions). The existing 9 state-classifier fixtures from buildFixtureCases still run untouched and still pass.\n  - 'node scripts/check-v3-request-flow-smoke.mjs' exit=0 (mode=static+fixture, same fixture count). Static blueprint + Rust-handler + MCP-schema validation paths unchanged.\n  - 'node scripts/check-v3-code-isomorphism-complete.mjs' exit=0 (7 surfaces graduated, 8 per-surface checkers passed). The aggregate gate runs check-v3-request-flow-smoke.mjs without flags so the new opt-in path never activates inside the gate.\n  - 'node scripts/check-v3-request-flow-smoke.mjs --live-ipc --restart-during-dispatch' (synthetic, no daemon) exits 2 with both validation errors before any IO, proving the gate fires before live IPC is attempted. Default --live-ipc + --execute-real-dispatch (no restart flag) is unchanged: the new restart_recovery_plan block is only entered when opts.restartDuringDispatch is true.\n  - perl NUL-byte audit on scripts/check-v3-request-flow-smoke.mjs: clean.\n\nFollow-up (NOT in this shard):\n  - Live execution of the 5-step plan (i.e., a future opt-in --confirm-restart that actually kills the daemon, polls the BoardTask through the recovery transitions, and asserts recovery_proof) is intentionally out of scope. The contract said 'Do not run a live daemon restart unless the parent explicitly asks after review.' Adding the executor in a follow-up wave is the natural next shard."
